WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.060
- [Mark] Mahogany. Where are you from?

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.430
- Originally, Chicago.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:06.340
- [Mark] And how long
you been out here in LA?

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.755
- I moved, I been out here
since I was two years old.

00:00:09.755 --> 00:00:11.580
I grew up in Long Beach.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.951
- [Mark] Oh, okay.

00:00:12.951 --> 00:00:13.920
- Yup.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.810
- [Mark] And how did you
end up holding a sign

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.803
on the freeway exit ramp?

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:24.150
- Well, I was on Section Eight,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.680
they um,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.660
I asked for an extension,

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.268
and they didn't give it to me.

00:00:28.268 --> 00:00:29.352
- [Mark] And what is Section Eight?

00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:31.024
- Section Eight is low-income housing

00:00:31.024 --> 00:00:32.250
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.430
- Also, HUD.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:34.263
- [Mark] Yep.

00:00:36.172 --> 00:00:38.443
- They actually made me homeless.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.963
They took my voucher, they
didn't give me an extension.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.510
- [Mark] Do you have kids, a family?

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.420
- I have one, I have a daughter.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.380
- [Mark] How old is she?

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.890
- She's 25.

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.109
- [Mark] Oh, really.

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:51.090
- Yep.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.020
I been homeless for about
five years now, since 2015.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.390
- [Mark] You're the best
dressed five year old-

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.980
- Well, you know, this is my motto,

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:00.813
just 'cause you're homeless,

00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:03.032
don't mean you have to
look like you're homeless.

00:01:03.032 --> 00:01:04.007
- [Mark] You look great.

00:01:04.007 --> 00:01:05.497
- You know, looks are
deceiving, so thank you.

00:01:08.135 --> 00:01:12.970
And then, I was staying
with some of her family,

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.390
and then they had to move,

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.353
so it's like getting put out twice.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:21.233
And then, here I am.

00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:24.330
No where to go.

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.190
- [Mark] Where do you sleep at night?

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.440
- [Mahagony] In an alley.

00:01:28.739 --> 00:01:29.730
- [Mark] So you're not
doing any of the drugs

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:31.412
that are here on the street?

00:01:31.412 --> 00:01:33.790
- [Mahagony] Uh no, I do
indulge in marijuana though.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:36.270
- [Mark] Yeah, but that's not as hard core

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.243
as some of the stuff here on Skid Row.

00:01:38.243 --> 00:01:39.076
- [Mahagony] No, no.

00:01:39.076 --> 00:01:41.560
- [Mark] And you're just a mile
away from Skid Row, roughly?

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.260
- [Mahagony] Yeah, I'm
not that far from it

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.650
but don't really want to be over there,

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.379
because it's crazy (laughs)

00:01:47.379 --> 00:01:48.500
- [Mark] Smart move, smart move.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:53.500
- [Mahagony] Um so, I also
have a significant other so...

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:56.733
We are in that alley.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.880
My story is...

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.429
- [Mark] How did you end up without a job?

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:08.780
- [Mahagony] Just going
through bein' evicted

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:12.723
by the people who gave
me the voucher, you know.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.130
Well not really being evicted,

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.283
I was asked to move.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:21.423
And then I moved, but I
didn't move to anywhere.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.340
I didn't have no where to go.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.630
But my daughter's people
actually took me in

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:29.320
after I sat in the car,

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.070
I slept in the car at first,

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.980
when I first became homeless.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.300
So then they took me in for a little bit,

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.340
and after that, they had to move.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.363
So everybody had to go their own way,

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.023
so I was like permanently
without a roof over my head.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.464
But I've had a troubled
childhood all my life

00:02:49.464 --> 00:02:51.256
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:02:51.256 --> 00:02:56.256
- My parents were married,
they both are from Chicago.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:02.310
I think on my dad's side

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:05.390
there's something going on in the genes,

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.343
that's genetic, hereditary,
but I don't know what.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.573
So he child molested me,

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:21.053
and it really made my brain go haywire.

00:03:22.111 --> 00:03:23.143
- [Mark] What age?

00:03:23.143 --> 00:03:23.976
- I didn't know-

00:03:23.976 --> 00:03:28.230
I was, I was a pre-teen
or in single digits.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:31.063
I was maybe eight, nine, maybe ten.

00:03:31.938 --> 00:03:34.030
- [Mark] Do you remember it?

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:34.870
- Yes, I do.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:35.703
Some of it.

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:38.340
I don't know how long he was doin' it

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.860
because he was don't it to me in my sleep,

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.810
when I was sleeping,
you know, fondling me.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:49.810
And after that, I don't know
how long he's done that to me,

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.963
I have more questions to ask him.

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:56.580
- [Mark] So your parents
are still married?

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:58.302
- No, they're not.

00:03:58.302 --> 00:04:01.647
My mother divorced him, you know.

00:04:01.647 --> 00:04:03.290
And that's a totally different story.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:08.065
My dad is an atheist, he
doesn't believe in God,

00:04:08.065 --> 00:04:10.113
he believes in the universe.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.680
But I think something happened to him.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:17.870
Because to me, that's not normal.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.910
You don't do that to a normal person.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.950
I mean you don't do that to anybody,

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:23.550
that's something that's taught.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:24.940
That's a learned behavior

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:29.940
that nobody takes upon
to say that it's wrong,

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:35.403
so it happened to me, he did that to me.

00:04:36.363 --> 00:04:38.970
As a kid, as an adolescent growing up,

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:43.231
I was like a wild child, promiscuous.

00:04:43.231 --> 00:04:44.064
- [Mark] Did you have
brothers and sisters?

00:04:44.064 --> 00:04:47.200
- Yes, I have one sister and two brothers.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.423
- [Mark] Do you think
anything happened with them?

00:04:48.423 --> 00:04:51.570
- I don't know, I have no idea,

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.773
and if it did, they didn't tell me.

00:04:54.773 --> 00:04:57.083
But you never know.

00:05:00.559 --> 00:05:02.041
- [Mark] Have you spoken
to your dad about it?

00:05:02.041 --> 00:05:05.370
- I've talked to him
once, briefly, about it,

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.800
and he told me because
he was in the industry,

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.940
the entertainment industry,

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.890
and maybe drugs or alcohol was involved,

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:18.640
that still doesn't justify
why he did that to his only,

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.083
his daughter, his firstborn daughter.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.290
He never taught me about my worth,

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.457
he never taught me about men,

00:05:27.457 --> 00:05:28.738
and that is the first man

00:05:28.738 --> 00:05:31.500
that is supposed to teach
you about the world,

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.620
and the men in it.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:33.630
And he never did that,

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.770
I had to learn by myself.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.483
And I'm still learning, so.

00:05:39.165 --> 00:05:40.480
- [Mark] How old are you?

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:41.543
- I am 42.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.330
And I never thought in the (sniffs)

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.050
in life today that I would be the one

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.590
holding the sign begging for money.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.010
I was ashamed at first,

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:55.450
but you know I have to eat too, you know,

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.183
and looks are very deceiving.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.373
I try to ignore some of the comments,

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.600
it's kinda hard but I do,

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.155
- [Mark] Its gotta be grating.

00:06:05.155 --> 00:06:07.605
- If I had some pennies,
I'd make it hail on 'em.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:14.023
But I don't resort to violence.

00:06:14.862 --> 00:06:16.213
- [Mark] Have you ever
had a job as an adult?

00:06:16.213 --> 00:06:17.983
- Yes I did, I had a job.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:22.720
And it seems like once my
voucher was taken from me,

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.910
it just, everything, like resurfaced,

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:28.480
just like, my whole life, just resurfaced,

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.595
like out of nowhere.

00:06:30.595 --> 00:06:34.157
And it was a wild rollercoaster ride,

00:06:34.157 --> 00:06:36.212
and I'm still on it,

00:06:36.212 --> 00:06:39.710
but hopefully soon, slowly but surely,

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.893
I'll be off of it.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:46.320
So, I'm happy, I'm very happy that

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.545
I didn't have to really sell my,

00:06:48.545 --> 00:06:49.630
I didn't sell my soul to the streets,

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.470
I eat-- 'cause I do get a GR check,

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.540
but that's just not enough to eat

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.880
for a whole month, every month,

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:01.880
so I resort to either going
recycling or I'll beg for money

00:07:07.699 --> 00:07:08.560
and I'm not ashamed

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.395
because there are a lot of

00:07:10.395 --> 00:07:11.540
wonderful people out there that helped me,

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:14.543
that helps me every day
when I do go out there.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:19.890
I try not to wear it out
though because I'm not greedy.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.220
Greed will get you in trouble,

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.010
so my motto is 'go when I need it'.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:27.150
- [Mark] So there are people
that would look at you and go,

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:29.553
she looks totally competent,
and she's sitting there with a-

00:07:29.553 --> 00:07:32.580
- 'You don't need to do
that, you can get a job'

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.674
- [Mark] And your answer to that is?

00:07:34.674 --> 00:07:36.097
- You don't know my background,

00:07:36.097 --> 00:07:37.630
you don't know the things
that I've been through,

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:42.313
and another thing is that I have a,

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.720
well they call it a disease,

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.513
but my disc is degenerating in my back,

00:07:48.858 --> 00:07:51.970
so sometimes I can't walk,
and it comes with sciatic pain

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:55.313
so it's on my nerve, and
sometimes I can't walk.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:08:00.540
If I bend over, it hurts,
if I sit too long, it hurts.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.560
So if my spine is out of whack,

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:06.890
it'll be thrown off
until it's back in place.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:11.040
And sometimes it takes like
a month, maybe two months.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.510
So I have two things going on,

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:15.570
because now I go,

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.860
I'm in mental health,

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:19.817
I have a mental health, I
have a therapist, but...

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.403
- [Mark] What kind of
disorder do you have,

00:08:25.403 --> 00:08:26.853
or what do they call it?

00:08:26.853 --> 00:08:27.840
- I wasn't diagnosed just yet,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.180
but I when I went down to the
Fifth Street Mental Health,

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:35.770
Downtown LA Mental Health, they said PTSD.

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:39.710
But I have anxiety, and I
know this, I'm depressed,

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:41.850
I don't, I barely be
wantin' to get out of bed,

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:44.620
never really wanted to get out
of bed when I was growin' up

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.150
as an adolescent, up until now.

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.030
You know, it's kinda hard
to get out of the bed.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.360
- [Mark] How much do you think

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.780
what happened to you with
your dad when you were young

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:54.713
played a part?

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.383
In your depression? Your anxiety?

00:08:58.383 --> 00:09:01.627
- That is, that was the
part. That was the whole,

00:09:01.627 --> 00:09:06.627
That's what, why I am who I am today.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.765
Because of that,

00:09:08.765 --> 00:09:09.865
and I don't have shit.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:14.370
But, I have a lot of love in my heart,

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:19.370
and I love people, and my
outlook is totally different,

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.200
and I know everybody has a story,

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.780
and the majority of their
stories have something to do with

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:31.160
something sexual happening to them,

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:36.080
and it's crazy how people
just swept it under the rug,

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.945
you know back then, I
mean I went to school,

00:09:38.945 --> 00:09:39.800
I have an Associates' degree,

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.603
so I took Black history,
I took psychology,

00:09:45.812 --> 00:09:47.660
so a lot of people swept a
lot of things under the rug,

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:50.260
and closed down a lot of mental healths.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:51.850
We need a lot of them back open,

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:54.630
for people like me and people
that's worse than me actually,

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:57.000
'cause there's a lot
of people that's worse,

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.244
the things that happened to them,

00:09:59.244 --> 00:10:01.380
that's worse than what happened to me, so.

00:10:02.322 --> 00:10:03.877
- [Mark] So it's all bad.

00:10:03.877 --> 00:10:04.753
- It is all bad.

00:10:04.753 --> 00:10:06.486
- [Mark] It all weakens the system.

00:10:06.486 --> 00:10:10.170
- The mind, the spirit, the health.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:15.170
It does a great deal of weakening
on the human body, period.

00:10:18.545 --> 00:10:19.393
And it's sad.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.020
You would think that
somebody that loves you

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:24.883
would actually really protect you,

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.083
but those are the ones
that really harm you.

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:31.589
And I deal with it every day,

00:10:31.589 --> 00:10:33.613
I deal with it every day.

00:10:33.613 --> 00:10:35.430
And relationships are extra hard.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.373
- [Mark] I bet.

00:10:36.373 --> 00:10:38.623
- Yeah, because in reality,

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:47.190
I dislike some of the things
that men do, you know.

00:10:49.447 --> 00:10:52.130
But again, what they do, some of 'em,

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:55.840
it's something that's
taught, that's what they see.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:58.360
They've seen it, they've
seen anything that

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:03.793
whatever they do to women,
or that was done to me,

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:09.720
physical abuse, mental
abuse, emotional abuse,

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:17.370
I can't even be, I can't even
emotionally support myself

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:20.390
because I'm all messed up.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:23.393
Because I get so angry
so fast, and frustrated.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.483
Not just with me, just with life period.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:35.190
And people that know me, probably
don't know this about me,

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.323
you know, 'cause only certain ones get,

00:11:40.861 --> 00:11:43.060
only certain chosen ones get the,

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:48.060
listen to me talk about me.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:53.043
So, it's crazy.

00:11:54.102 --> 00:11:56.510
And don't mess with,
don't date somebody who

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:58.543
has a problem worse than you.

00:11:59.759 --> 00:12:00.592
It's hard.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:06.360
My daughter tells me
'stop looking for love,

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.747
love is overrated'.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:13.530
But I guess when something happens to you,

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.283
like what happened to me,

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:21.240
and you never talk, you
just go looking for it

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:23.593
and sometimes it's not
good to look for it.

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.488
I tell you one thing,

00:12:28.488 --> 00:12:31.340
if this relationship that
I'm in doesn't work out,

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.777
I think I'm gonna be by myself
for the rest of my life.

00:12:33.777 --> 00:12:35.253
'cause I don't have time,

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.450
I already have to take the time out

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:39.970
for myself to try to heal,

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:44.124
it's even harder when
you're dealing with somebody

00:12:44.124 --> 00:12:47.913
that's broker, broken, more than myself.

00:12:51.523 --> 00:12:53.730
- [Mark] It's hard just
taking care of yourself.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:54.563
- Yeah, I mean,

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.490
the things that people give me,

00:12:57.490 --> 00:13:01.290
I don't just enjoy it myself,

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:05.090
I help other people to that's
in the same situation as I am.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:08.633
So the little money that
I do get goes a long ways.

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:13.650
Sometimes I'm told 'why
do you help people?

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:16.600
Why don't you just help yourself?
Nobody's gonna help you.'

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.360
I ignore it, I still do it.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.060
That's probably my problem.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:24.898
One of my problems.

00:13:24.898 --> 00:13:26.518
- [Mark] Yeah, but when
you're helping other people,

00:13:26.518 --> 00:13:27.675
you're helping yourself.

00:13:27.675 --> 00:13:29.247
- Yeah, and I feel it,

00:13:29.247 --> 00:13:30.589
even though people tell me

00:13:30.589 --> 00:13:31.700
I should just look out for myself,

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.443
I just can't see myself doin' that.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:38.900
Because actually somebody
took me in, you know,

00:13:38.900 --> 00:13:40.530
and they helped me,

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:43.393
so why not help somebody else.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:48.223
Anybody that's out on the
streets and needs help,

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:52.173
even if I'm on the streets,
I can still help somebody

00:13:52.173 --> 00:13:54.800
because I can, I know how to cook,

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.443
so at least I know they'll
be eatin' something good,

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.000
and actually will remember me by

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.803
what they ate that I cooked.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.383
It's a, to me, it's a win-win situation.

00:14:07.779 --> 00:14:10.499
- [Mark] Where would you like
to see yourself in five years?

00:14:10.499 --> 00:14:12.283
- Oh, in five years, I would love,

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:15.380
if I can stay focused,

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:18.040
I would love to have a
nonprofit organization

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:21.053
that will tend and help the homeless.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:24.460
Make sure they have a good meal,

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.563
because I know I know how to cook,

00:14:26.563 --> 00:14:28.990
even though put a roof,
or tent, over their head,

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:30.720
because a lot of people that's homeless,

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:33.850
they so used to bein' out in the streets,

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:36.390
to where sometimes they won't come back,

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.943
they won't go back to what they were so,

00:14:40.265 --> 00:14:41.780
what they were used to before they became

00:14:42.727 --> 00:14:43.970
the person that they are today.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:46.880
So, some type of facility,

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.610
if you want to sleep outside in a tent,

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:50.022
you go ahead,

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:54.050
at least you know that
you can you have a meal,

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:57.260
you can even have porta potties outside,

00:14:57.260 --> 00:14:58.680
I mean, that's just something that

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:00.290
I've thought about, you know.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.231
(sirens)

00:15:01.231 --> 00:15:02.800
Or, the people that's like me,

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:07.440
that's used to being in a,
with a roof over their head,

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:11.110
and use the bathroom regularly,

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.800
instead of in a paint bucket,

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.293
a five gallon paint bucket,

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:18.100
or going to fetch your water,

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:20.180
at least there'd be running water,

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:24.470
you know, that's what I would
like to do within five years,

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:26.890
but I gotta stay focused so,

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:28.970
and it's kinda hard
sometimes to stay focused,

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.940
'cause I get so drained and tired and

00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:36.620
don't want to get out the bed,
and sleepy, it's a struggle.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.820
And it's been a struggle
all my life though.

